  "_doc": {
    "about": "Inbox bundles, run by shared/src/list-model.spec.ts and Android :core LabelGroupFixturesTest (America/New_York; times are local).",
    "inbox": "inboxSections(threads, now, bundleLabels): STARRED threads go to Pinned; the rest, newest first, fold by label (a bundle label with two or more of them becomes one group holding all of them) and each entry lands in the time section of its newest thread. A section whose threads all moved into a newer bundle is left out. Entries are a thread id, or label[ids] for a group. held (optional) is what open threads and bundles keep until they close (see held-place-fixtures.json): a held thread sorts and sections by its held date, sits with the pinned threads or not as held, and when held as single stays out of bundles; held.pins (optional) holds the focused thread's pinning only: it sits with the pinned threads or not as held, and otherwise by its own date and labels; a held bundle sorts and sections by its held date, stays a bundle however few threads it has, and takes any thread carrying its label; left with none it stays too, unless its label is in exhausted (optional: bundle labels Gmail has no more of), when it leaves the list. todoThreads (optional) are the threads whose email has a todo: such a thread is never in a bundle, nor counts toward one, and has its own row.",
    "plain": "plainSections(threads, now, held): any other mailbox, newest first in time sections; a held thread at its held date.",
    "preview": "groupShownCount(threads, showAll): an open bundle shows its first 5 threads, then \"Show N more\" for the hidden rest; all once asked."
  },
